# Templates for which a `package-update` issue automatically triggers an
# autobump. One package name per line, '#' for comments.
#
# A template qualifies when both autobump halves work on it:
#   * its `update` file yields a candidate version (.github/scripts/detect-update.sh)
#   * its distfiles URL derives from ${version} and every distfile is a plain
#     sha256 download (.github/scripts/bump-template.sh)
#
# Never list a symlinked alias: an alias is a second name for one directory,
# so bumping it would rewrite the target's template. lint-autobump-symlinks.sh
# enforces that.
#
# To re-run the automation for an issue, edit the issue body (e.g. bump the
# version) — the workflow re-triggers on `edited` events.
